# OptiQ harness workflow

Target repository: `/Users/stewartbarteau/Desktop/old-q4-extras/agent-harness`.

Read its `AGENTS.md` before every change. It is a local Rust tool host with a TypeScript agent loop and existing skills/workflows. Use its owned tools and workflows rather than creating parallel, unrestricted equivalents.

Required constraints:

- Keep Cargo offline: use `cargo build --offline` or `cargo test --offline`.
- Do not run `npm install`, `pip`, `brew`, `sudo`, remote clients, disk tools, or arbitrary network tooling inside the harness.
- Do not load a model or import MLX. OptiQ already serves on `127.0.0.1:8000`; preserve its sampler card and do not start another server.
- Keep `ts/agent.mjs` free of request-level sampler fields.
- Keep the session root jailed. New tools must be owned by a skill and be bounded like the Rust host.

Use the existing workflows before ad hoc steps:

```sh
# agent-harness/README.md — discovery and smoke verification
export PATH="/opt/homebrew/bin:$PATH"
node ts/cli.mjs workflow orient
node ts/cli.mjs workflow fix-and-verify
cargo test --offline
node ts/smoke.mjs
```

For browser checks, keep Playwright outside the harness and point it only at a local test surface. Record that separation in the test report.
